{"audit_run_id":"audit:b961d633d97a468293944c47ec266aa8","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":91,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"The data file is `gari_fermentation_batches.csv`. It holds 40 data rows plus a header row."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"One row is one fermentation batch: a single 20 kg unit of grated cassava mash fermented in its own"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"press bag and sampled once, 72 hours after fermentation started. Each batch is measured once, so"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"there are no repeated measures. Twenty batches were fermented with a back-slopped inoculum carried"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"over from a previous successful batch, and twenty were left to ferment spontaneously with no added"},{"end_column":10,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"inoculum."},{"end_column":28,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"| Column | Meaning | Unit |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":170,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"| `batch_id` | Batch identifier, unique across the study. `BS-01` to `BS-20` are the back-slopped batches, `SP-01` to `SP-20` the spontaneous ones. | none (text label) |"},{"end_column":121,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"| `fermentation_treatment` | Group assignment. Exactly two values: `back_slopped` and `spontaneous`. | none (category) |"},{"end_column":189,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"| `total_cyanogenic_potential_mg_hcn_eq_per_kg_dw` | Declared outcome 1. Total cyanogenic potential of the finished gari. | milligrams hydrogen cyanide equivalent per kilogram dry weight |"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"| `ph_72h_ph_units` | Declared outcome 2. pH of the mash measured at 72 hours. | pH units |"},{"end_column":185,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"| `titratable_acidity_percent_lactic_acid` | Declared outcome 3. Titratable acidity of the mash at 72 hours, expressed as lactic acid. | percent lactic acid (g lactic acid per 100 g) |"},{"end_column":110,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"| `moisture_content_percent` | Declared outcome 4. Moisture content of the finished gari. | percent by mass |"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"The outcome columns appear in the order the four outcomes were declared in the study plan. Every"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"batch has a value in every outcome column, and there are no blank cells. The measurements are"},{"end_column":69,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"invented for this project, not collected from a real processing run."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"Each group holds 20 batches. Every outcome is compared between the two groups with the same test, a"},{"end_column":35,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"two-sided Welch two-sample t-test."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"The four declared outcomes form one family, so the family-wise error rate is controlled. The family"},{"end_column":83,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"size is 4 and the family-wise level is 0.05. The Sidak per-comparison threshold is"},{"end_column":41,"end_line":34,"start_column":5,"start_line":34,"text":"1 - (1 - 0.05) ** (1 / 4) = 0.012741"},{"end_column":82,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"Every verdict below compares that outcome's p-value with 0.012741, not with 0.05."},{"end_column":74,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"Group sizes are 20 back-slopped and 20 spontaneous for all four outcomes."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"Mean 9.4500 for back-slopped, 12.0500 for spontaneous. The back-slopped batches are 2.6000 lower."},{"end_column":101,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"t = -3.4973, p = 0.00131933. This is below the 0.012741 threshold, so the difference is significant."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"Mean 4.0245 for back-slopped, 4.2790 for spontaneous. The back-slopped batches are 0.2545 lower."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":50,"start_column":1,"start_line":50,"text":"t = -6.3043, p = 3.07609e-07. This is below the 0.012741 threshold, so the difference is"},{"end_column":13,"end_line":51,"start_column":1,"start_line":51,"text":"significant."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":55,"start_column":1,"start_line":55,"text":"Mean 0.9150 for back-slopped, 0.7975 for spontaneous. The back-slopped batches are 0.1175 higher."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":56,"start_column":1,"start_line":56,"text":"t = 3.0844, p = 0.00402361. This is below the 0.012741 threshold, so the difference is significant."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":60,"start_column":1,"start_line":60,"text":"Mean 9.5150 for back-slopped, 9.5700 for spontaneous. The back-slopped batches are 0.0550 lower."},{"end_column":90,"end_line":61,"start_column":1,"start_line":61,"text":"t = -0.2354, p = 0.815186. This is above the 0.012741 threshold, so the difference is not"},{"end_column":13,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"significant."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":66,"start_column":1,"start_line":66,"text":"On this data, processors should use the back-slopped inoculum. Back-slopped batches finished with a"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":67,"start_column":1,"start_line":67,"text":"lower total cyanogenic potential, a lower pH and a higher titratable acidity than spontaneous"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":68,"start_column":1,"start_line":68,"text":"batches, and all three of those differences hold up against the Sidak threshold of 0.012741."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":69,"start_column":1,"start_line":69,"text":"Moisture content came out about the same in both groups, so the choice of treatment does not appear"},{"end_column":40,"end_line":70,"start_column":1,"start_line":70,"text":"to change how dry the finished gari is."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":72,"start_column":1,"start_line":72,"text":"Two limits are worth stating. The measurements are invented rather than collected, so the numbers"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":73,"start_column":1,"start_line":73,"text":"above describe this synthetic data set and not real processing lines. The study also sampled each"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":74,"start_column":1,"start_line":74,"text":"batch once at 72 hours, so it says nothing about how the two treatments differ earlier or later in"},{"end_column":14,"end_line":75,"start_column":1,"start_line":75,"text":"fermentation."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:9b49bf522be493033fd1","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:20f32974c6db925785faca46fbeb2550960bbedf1c8d79e25b78772f27cf66dd","end_line":75,"locator":"report.md:1-75","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
